al", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bilalmuzamil-sketch/Manual-test-Cases/claude/heic-upload-iphone-test-sz7h5p/build/sv9087-credit-term-2026-08-27/evidence/EX-C-credit-hold-annotated.png"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check C \u2014 \u201cCREDIT HOLD\u201d / \u201ccredit hold\u201d / padded all show the Credit Hold banner, disable Create Invoice, and show the tooltip \u201cCannot invoice this customer. Customer is on Credit Hold\u201d.", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}]}, {"type": "mediaSingle", "attrs": {"layout": "full-width"}, "content": [{"type": "media", "attrs": {"type": "external", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bilalmuzamil-sketch/Manual-test-Cases/claude/heic-upload-iphone-test-sz7h5p/build/sv9087-credit-term-2026-08-27/evidence/EX-D-charge-account-comparison.png"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check D \u2014 cash-on-delivery (cod / COD / whitespace-only) withholds the Charge Account button and payment method; Net 30 / Due On Receipt / Prepaid still show it. Same work order and invoice, differing only by the customer's credit term.", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}]}, {"type": "mediaSingle", "attrs": {"layout": "full-width"}, "content": [{"type": "media", "attrs": {"type": "external", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bilalmuzamil-sketch/Manual-test-Cases/claude/heic-upload-iphone-test-sz7h5p/build/sv9087-credit-term-2026-08-27/evidence/E-invoice-created-payment.png"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check E \u2014 invoice created for the NET 30 customer: the document shows Terms NET 30 and a due date 30 days after the issue date.", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}]}, {"type": "mediaSingle", "attrs": {"layout": "full-width"}, "content": [{"type": "media", "attrs": {"type": "external", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bilalmuzamil-sketch/Manual-test-Cases/claude/heic-upload-iphone-test-sz7h5p/build/sv9087-credit-term-2026-08-27/evidence/F-receive-screen.png"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check F \u2014 vendor credit term \u201cNET 30\u201d: Accept Delivery records the delivery due date 30 days out.", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}]}, {"type": "mediaSingle", "attrs": {"layout": "full-width"}, "content": [{"type": "media", "attrs": {"type": "external", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bilalmuzamil-sketch/Manual-test-Cases/claude/heic-upload-iphone-test-sz7h5p/build/sv9087-credit-term-2026-08-27/evidence/G-quickbooks-admin.png"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Check G \u2014 QuickBooks is connected on this org, but the invoice sync currently fails on a tax-code configuration issue unrelated to this ticket (see notes). The term logic is unit-covered.", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}]}, {"type": "rule"}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Technical details for developers", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Environment: ", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "sv9087.qa.shopview.com, build v26.35.4-b216483. Terms seeded via POST /api/customers/change and (vendor) POST /api/parts-catalogue/change-vendor with the full record + a mis-spelled credit_term. A customer contact is required for the invoice preview to render (without one, GET /api/invoices/{wo}/details returns 500 and Create Invoice stays disabled)."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A: ", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "WO S9087-15890, term \u201cNET 30\u201d. Draft due date Aug 27 \u2192 Sep 26; invoice date \u2192 09/15/2026 gives due Oct 15, 2026. No error boundary; term sweep across 7 spellings produced 0 blanks / 0 errors."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "B: ", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "Typed 13/01/2026 into date_input_invoice_date \u2014 issue and due dates unchanged on screen, no new invoice/estimate request fired."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "D: ", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "Verified in the auto-opened payment dialog after Create Invoice (reverse + re-create per term). button_charge_account absent for cod / COD / whitespace-only; present for Net 30 / Due On Receipt / Prepaid (pre-selected as the method for the first two)."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "E/F: ", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "Created invoice document due date = issue + 30; vendor Accept Delivery due date = invoice date + 30 (2026-08-27 \u2192 2026-09-26)."}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "G (QuickBooks): ", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "QB is connected on org d55bc308 (QuickBooks admin: Deposit sync enabled, mappings present). The invoice sync currently fails before the term step with \u201cInvalid Line TaxCode ... Valid line TaxCodes for US should be TAX or NON. Supplied value: 3\u201d (Canadian GST vs a US QB company) and QB sync is paused for deposits and fees/discounts \u2014 all unrelated to this fix. The credit-term de-dup itself resolves through the same case-folding proven live in checks C and F, and is covered by the unit tests (38 inputs through the real CreditTerms class). A live QuickBooks Online Terms-list check is deferred until a QB-verifiable environment is available."}]}]}]}]}
